    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d43">

                <pb facs="0097" n="69" xml:id="pg69"/>

                <head>43. Diary Entry by the President<anchor n="1" xml:id="d43-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1956-01-19"><hi rendition="#italic">January 19,
                        1956</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Ambassador Conant came to see me to bring me personal messages from Chancellor
                        Adenauer<anchor n="2" xml:id="d43-f2"
                    /> and the report that the Chancellor’s health, at 81, seems to be improving
                    daily. He also expressed to me his (Conant’s) great concern in establishing in
                    Europe a six-power community for handling of activities in nuclear science in
                    that region. He points out that in some of these countries activities could well
                    go underground if we did not move in the direction of the community development.
                    I agreed with him.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d43-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d43-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Eisenhower Library, Whitman File,
                    DDE Diaries. Secret.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d43-f2" n="2" xml:id="d43-f2-content">
                <p>No oral or written messages from Adenauer
                    have been found in Department of State files or the Eisenhower Library.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
